# Health data — never commit. These are a real person's physiological record:
# recovery, HRV, skin temperature, blood oxygen, sleep staging, and 550 free-text
# journal notes. Paired with timestamps and a timezone they are de-anonymising.
# `physiological_cycles.csv` is also the app's bundled import resource, so a fresh
# clone will not build until you supply one — your own export, or a header-only
# placeholder. Recipe in README.md §Building.
# The directory is named for the producer, because the CSVs in it came from WHOOP —
# `ZeroFasting/` beside it is the same arrangement for a different app's export. The
# pattern names the subdirectory and not `**`, deliberately: a bare `*.csv` under
# `Resources/` would also swallow a future resource that is not health data.
ios/Sources/Whoopsy/Data/Resources/Whoop/*.csv

# Zero Fasting Data
ios/Sources/Whoopsy/Data/Resources/ZeroFasting

# Mapbox credentials — never commit.
# `Mapbox.local.xcconfig` holds the PUBLIC (`pk.…`) access token, which is the only
# copy of it: at the owner's request it lives outside the tree. `ios/App/Config/Mapbox.xcconfig`
# is the committed base and carries no token — it ends with `#include? "Mapbox.local.xcconfig"`,
# the *optional* include, so a clone without this file still builds and simply gets the
# pre-feature behaviour (an empty `MBXAccessToken`, `MapboxSetup.configure()` returning
# `false`, and the route card drawing `MapKit`). Recipe in README.md §Building.
# The SECRET token (`sk.…`, `Downloads:Read`) must never be written here either —
# it is a build-time credential for SwiftPM and lives in `~/.netrc` only.
ios/App/Config/Mapbox.local.xcconfig

# Cloud sync backend — never commit.
backend/node_modules
backend/.wrangler

# Testing scratch — never commit. `tmp/` is where everything produced *while testing* goes,
# so that nothing is written outside the repo and nothing local reaches a commit:
#
#   tmp/screenshots/  simulator captures taken while verifying a change
#   tmp/scratch/      one-off probe sources and build logs
#   tmp/backups/      simulator-container SQLite copies
#   tmp/build/        build output — SwiftPM's scratch path (`scripts/test.sh`) and Xcode's
#                     derived data (`make ios`). Pure output; `make clean` removes it.
#
# The pattern is `/tmp/*` and not `/tmp/`, deliberately. Excluding the directory itself
# stops git descending into it, and the tracked README below it could then never be
# re-included — the rule is "you cannot un-ignore a file whose parent directory is ignored".
tmp/*
!tmp/README.md